// The body is wrapped only to keep its SOURCE TEXT: a block with no |params| that
// mentions _1 / _2 takes them as its parameters, and Ruby decides the block's arity
// from the HIGHEST one mentioned (which is what makes { _1 + _2 } destructure a
// two-element item while { _1 * 2 } gets the item whole). Nothing else can tell them
// apart, so makeBlock scans this text.
BlockBody   <~~ var bb = pop(); push({body: bb.body, btext: up.in}) ~~>
